  "notes": "An American trio making vocal-led dance-pop across tropical, future-bass and house modes. `confidence` is low because the research rates the entry medium-low — \"era and sub-genre set documented; parameters are convention-derived and marked\" — and its harmony claim carries an explicit `[LOW-CONF]`, repeated here. The kit is written as the composite the entry describes: \"a soft four-square kick with clap on 2&4 and offbeat shaker in the tropical mode; a half-time-feeling snare-on-3 drop in the future-bass mode. Riser-and-snare-roll builds.\" A single-mode model states one kick, so this one keeps the four-square anchors and the 2&4 backbeat of the tropical side and lets the syncopation and the ghost set on the fourth beat carry the future-bass drop — a composite, marked INFERRED. What the entry does give as a fact is the melodic identity: \"plucked and bell leads plus chopped vocal hooks as the drop's melody; they sing on their own records as well as hosting guests, so the topline and the chopped hook are frequently the same voice\", which is why the countermelody is a bell echo doubling the lead at a high density rather than an independent answer. Harmony is \"major and modal-major four-chord loops with maj7/add9 colour, kept static under the topline\", loops are 4 bars, and the bass is a detuned chord stack in the drop over a rounded tropical sub. ⚠ Every velocity, density and register above is INFERRED.",
